      "customfield_10012" : "0|i002x3:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{repository={count=1, dataType=repository}, json={\"cachedValue\":{\"errors\":[],\"summary\":{\"repository\":{\"overall\":{\"count\":1,\"lastUpdated\":\"2016-04-06T09:23:11.000-0400\",\"dataType\":\"repository\"},\"byInstanceType\":{\"oAuth-com.github.integration.production\":{\"count\":1,\"name\":\"GitHub\"},\"GitHub\":{\"count\":1,\"name\":\"GitHub\"}}}}},\"isStale\":true}}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For now - this comprises just specifying the stack size and the stack guardsize.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For AIX I see only one obvious way to set this (given use of the std::thread class which uses all teh defaults):",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// According to ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/ssw_aix_61/com.ibm.aix.performance/thread_supp_tun_params.htm"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/ssw_aix_61/com.ibm.aix.performance/thread_supp_tun_params.htm",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// Default: 98 304 bytes for 32-bit applications, 196 608 bytes for 64-bit applications.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// Range: Decimal integer values from 0 to 268 435 455 which will be rounded up to the nearest page (currently 4 096).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "if (sizeof (void*) == 4)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "{",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "static const char kStackSizeEnvVarSetting_[] = \"AIXTHREAD_STK=130000\";",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "DbgTrace (\"Setting env-var %s\", kStackSizeEnvVarSetting_);",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "and same for AIXTHREAD_GUARD..... (or some such).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "The trouble with this is its a bit of race - you modify global variables (setenv). Best to avoid if we can.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For Linux - I'm not sure.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "UNIX/Linux:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "gthread_create (_gthread_t threadid, void ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "strong"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "(func) (void",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "),void *_args)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "{ return ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "em"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "gthrw(pthread_create) (",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "_threadid, NULL, __func, __args)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "so construcint std::thread wtih libstdc++ just uses the default for posix_threads.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "MAYBE I can replace (link trick) - the default gthread_create function?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For windows - I'm also not sure how todo this. I'm not sure is imporant,a nd since I dont really know how to do it - back burtner for now.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
